{{!-- HOW TO LAY THE WAY OUT YOURSELF, under the picture it is about.

      There used to be a "Draw the way yourself" checkbox above the map, and the gestures were
      taught in the row beside it. The box is gone: a shift-click on the map lays a way, and the
      marks themselves are the mode (module/utils/custom-route.js `normalizeCustom`). What is left
      is the one thing a map cannot say for itself — nothing about a picture advertises that shift
      adds a leg — and it belongs UNDER the picture, where a reader looking for what a click will
      do is already looking, rather than in a row of controls above it.

      SHARED BY BOTH SURFACES, like the controls above and the readout below: the route step sets
      it under its own map, the "See the whole map" window under its viewport. One sentence, so the
      gesture cannot come to mean two different things depending on which window you are in.

      WHICH sentence is `ExpeditionDialog._drawState`'s to decide, off the same `canDrawHere` the
      two surfaces arm their pictures on — an invitation on a map that can start a way, the
      gestures once one is drawn here, and where the way actually is when it is drawn elsewhere.
      All this partial owns is where it sits.

      GM-only (`canDraw`), like the scene and site buttons above and for the same reason: drawing
      writes the trip into a world setting, which a player cannot do. A player gets the one thing
      that is still theirs to know, and only once there is a way: that the line on this map is
      somebody's own and the times beside it were measured rather than printed. --}}
{{#if journey.custom.canDraw}}
<div class="stonetop-journey-draw{{#if journey.custom.on}} is-on{{/if}}">
  <span class="stonetop-journey-drawhint">{{journey.custom.hint}}</span>
  {{!-- COUNTED, not conditioned on this map: the marks are on the trip, so "start over" is offered
        from the other tab too — a way that plainly has something to start over from should not
        have the button go missing on it. --}}
  {{#if journey.custom.count}}
  <button type="button" class="stonetop-journey-clear-drawn" data-tooltip="{{journey.custom.clearTip}}">
    <i class="fas fa-rotate-left"></i> {{journey.custom.clearLabel}}
  </button>
  {{/if}}
</div>
{{else if journey.custom.on}}
<div class="stonetop-journey-draw is-on">
  <span class="stonetop-journey-drawhint">{{journey.custom.drawnNote}}</span>
</div>
{{/if}}
